CloudBurrow patch 47 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1456). Needs 0021 and 0022.

The bug: the engine had one time zone, UTC (patch 0022), so BigQuery's
project option default_time_zone, "the default time zone to use in time
zone-dependent GoogleSQL functions, when a time zone is not specified as
an argument", could not reach it. CloudBurrow's front wrote the zone into
the query text where the text showed a TIMESTAMP, and could not where it
did not: DATE(ts), STRING(ts), EXTRACT(HOUR FROM ts) and CAST(ts AS
STRING) of a column, DATE_TRUNC(ts, MONTH), CAST(d AS TIMESTAMP) stayed
in UTC.

The patch adds WithDefaultTimeZone(ctx, zone): a query run with it
- gives the zone to each call that takes one and is given none, where the
  resolved argument is a TIMESTAMP (DATE, DATETIME, TIME, STRING, EXTRACT,
  TIMESTAMP_TRUNC, FORMAT_TIMESTAMP; DATE_TRUNC and DATETIME_TRUNC of a
  TIMESTAMP run as TIMESTAMP_TRUNC) or where it makes one (TIMESTAMP(x),
  PARSE_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_DATE, CURRENT_DATETIME, CURRENT_TIME);
- does a cast between TIMESTAMP and STRING, DATE, DATETIME or TIME in the
  zone (googlesqlite_cast's fifth argument; a FORMAT cast with no AT TIME
  ZONE gets it too);
- reads a TIMESTAMP literal with no zone, and a string literal cast to
  TIMESTAMP, in the zone (applyNaiveTimestampIn, before patch 0021's UTC
  pass);
- analyzes with literal casts left to the run time
  (SetFoldLiteralCast(false), a second shared AnalyzerOptions): the
  analyzer folds CAST(TIMESTAMP '...' AS STRING) and CAST(DATE '...' AS
  TIMESTAMP) in its own zone, which go-googlesql can build only as UTC.
"" and "UTC" change nothing. Measured on the emulator with patches 0001
to 0041, in America/New_York: STRING(ts) of a column holding
2020-01-01 03:00:00 UTC was "2020-01-01 03:00:00+00", now
"2019-12-31 22:00:00-05"; default_time_zone_test.go has each form. Still
UTC: a string literal compared with, or coerced to, a TIMESTAMP column
(the analyzer coerces it).

